# A data breakpoint next to an instruction breakpoint, on the flash demo (start_in_flash):
# compute() writes g_result before it returns, so from the breakpoint at its first line (38)
# the next stop is the data breakpoint, after the store (the value is 46 then).
#
# Until probe-rs fork 149db65 the data breakpoint did not halt once an instruction breakpoint
# was armed (break after make next to break before make triggers, TriCore).

attach ../../dap-client/examples/tc275_demo_3cores.json
continue all
pause 0
wait stopped 0
watch g_result write
continue 0
wait stopped 0 reason data breakpoint within 3s
break ${AURIX_DEMO:-C:/work/aurix_tcf_demo}/src/demo.c:38
continue 0
wait stopped 0 reason breakpoint within 3s
continue 0
wait stopped 0 reason data breakpoint within 3s
expect g_result == 46
continue 0
wait stopped 0 reason breakpoint within 3s
continue 0
wait stopped 0 reason data breakpoint within 3s
expect g_result == 46
